    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0391" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.G35/52.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have just been informed by the Secretary of State that yesterday he appealed to
                    the newspapers of Habana to cease their campaign of abuse and that they all
                    promised to do so. He made it clear that there was no foundation for the attacks
                    on me and that the guilty papers will make a full apology. He asks that these
                    papers be not prosecuted in order to favor return to normal conditions; I
                    replied that the matter was not in my hands but awaited the decision of my
                    Government. Press attacks have practically ceased and the better class of papers
                    are becoming distinctly friendly. The Cuban Government denies to the press that
                    any message has been received from the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
